    "description": {
      "type": "/type/text",
      "value": "\"This is the story of how two brothers - Edouard and Andre Michelin - turned a sleepy, family tyre firm in the heart of rural France into one of the most innovative and successful industrial empires in the world. Edouard, a landscape painter at the Ecole des Beaux Arts, displayed an engineering genius for tyre-making and product innovation, whilst Andre, trained as an engineer, displayed a creative genius for advertising and marketing. Together they kick-started the world motor industry and created a tourist industry around the motor car and their now legendary \"Michelin Guides\". The Michelin history, as described here by Herbert Lottman, reveals insights into the development of this business.\"--Jacket."
